<title>UK: UK notes in circulation rise 6.5 pct.</title>
<headline>UK notes in circulation rise 6.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>British bank notes in circulation rose 6.5 percent in the week to June 4 over the equivalent year-ago week, the Bank of England said. Last week the annual adjusted rise was 6.0 percent. NOTES IN CIRCULATION (in rounded bln stg) -</p>
<p>				Latest week  pvs week	yr-ago week</p>
<p> Notes in circulation     21.56	  21.78	   20.24</p>
<p> Bankers' deposits	   2.49	   2.10	    2.018</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom 44 171 542 2774</p>
</text>
